   "speech": "“I can’t, sir… Would you believe it? I don’t sleep, I don’t eat, I’m turning into an idiot… I need it to take my mind off things, that’s what, sir! The moment you say those words, I’ll calm down… You talk and you talk, and then up it floats, that very thought… I’m afraid of it. Now, if you’d be so good as to listen… It must have been, oh, eight or nine days ago… Of course, we all think about it… This one will die, then another… About death, I mean… And how it all comes about, I tell you, how one thing hooks onto the next — it’s beyond all understanding… There I was, sitting by the window, reading a book, only I hadn’t much wish to read; it was getting on towards dinner. I sit there and I look… You know the kind of mood one gets into — at another moment I’d have spat and paid no attention… But just then my thoughts were wandering, it was warmish, such a quiet summer day… And along comes, I see, a woman with a babe in arms, a kerchief on her of red calico, bright red… Then a little girl of about seven ran past, a skinny little thing, with a ginger pigtail sticking out like a piglet’s tail… Allow me, sir… Then I see a gymnasium schoolgirl going by after her, then a lady, a very well-dressed lady, very proper, and behind her, if you please — a little old woman… There… you understand?”",
